 34MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34MG c  2013Do22: a 345-MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam was accelerated by the
 34MG2c  superconducting ring cyclotron (SRC) at RIKEN. secondary beams of      
 34MG3c  39Al+40Si and 37Al+36Mg were produced by the fragmentation of {+48}Ca  
 34MG4c  on a Be target and separated by the BigRIPS separator using the        
 34MG5c  B|r-|DE-B|r method. The secondary reaction target was 2.54-g/cm{+2}    
 34MG6c  thick carbon. The secondary reaction products {+34}Mg, {+36}Mg, and    
 34MG7c  {+38}Mg were identified by the magnetic spectrometer ZeroDegree using  
 34MG8c  the B|r-|DE-ToF method. |g rays in coincidence with {+34}Mg were       
 34MG9c  detected using the DALI2 array of 186 large NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured
 34MGAc  E|g with Doppler correction, I|g, and ({+34}Mg)|g-coin. Deduced levels.
 34MGBc  Compared with shell-model calculations using the SPDF-M effective      
 34MGCc  interaction.                                                           
